{
  "_id": "6b041f6b7510c4b9d7d90e35",
  "Package": "msPurity",
  "Type": "Package",
  "Title": "Tools for LC-MSn-Based Metabolomics: Precursor Ion Purity\nAssessment, Fragmentation Data and Spectral Tree Processing,\nand Spectral Matching",
  "Version": "1.99.8",
  "Date": "2026-11-22",
  "Authors@R": "c(\nperson(given = \"Thomas N.\", family = \"Lawson\",\nemail = \"thomas.nigel.lawson@gmail.com\", role = \"aut\",\ncomment = c(ORCID = \"0000-0002-5915-7980\")),\nperson(given = \"Ossama\", family = \"Edbali\",\nemail = \"o.edbali@bham.ac.uk\", role = c(\"aut\", \"cre\"),\ncomment = c(ORCID = \"0000-0003-0132-8668\")),\nperson(given = \"Ralf\", family = \"Weber\", role = c(\"aut\", \"ths\"),\ncomment = c(ORCID = \"0000-0002-8796-4771\")),\nperson(given = \"Martin\", family = \"Jones\", role = \"ctb\"),\nperson(given = \"Julien\", family = \"Saint-Vanne\", role = \"ctb\"),\nperson(given = \"Andris\", family = \"Jankevics\", role = \"ctb\"),\nperson(given = \"Mark\", family = \"Viant\", role = \"ths\"),\nperson(given = \"Warwick\", family = \"Dunn\", role = \"ths\"))",
  "URL": "https://github.com/computational-metabolomics/msPurity/",
  "Description": "Provides tools for precursor ion purity assessment,\nprocessing fragmentation data and spectral trees, and spectral\nmatching in LC-MSn-based metabolomics. Precursor ion purity\nestimates the contribution of a selected precursor to the\nsignal within its isolation window, using neighbouring MS1\nmeasurements for MS2 and linked parent fragmentation spectra\nfor higher MSn levels. Fragmentation spectra can be associated\nwith chromatographic features, filtered and averaged using\nacquisition-aware settings. Mass Spectral Trees link successive\nfragmentation spectra, while Precursor-Fragment Trees connect\nindividual precursor and product peaks. Spectral matching\ncompares measured or consensus spectra with experimental\nspectra and reference libraries, accounting for MS level,\nprecursor relationships and acquisition conditions. The\noptional BLINK method computes approximate cosine similarity as\ndescribed by Harwood et al. (2023)\n<doi:10.1038/s41598-023-40496-9>. Integration with 'Spectra'\nand 'xcms' connects spectrum handling and chromatographic\nfeature information. Parquet datasets link raw measurements,\nprocessed spectra and reference libraries, retaining feature\nassociations, processing settings and measurement provenance.\nReusable parameter objects and recorded processing history\nsupport reproducible analysis and reopening of processed\nresults. Spectrum selection, linked visualisation, library\nimport and export, and reporting of feature information and\nspectral matches support downstream interpretation and data\nexchange.",
